From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Open Arc Authors <dev@openarc.invalid>
Date: Sun, 25 Oct 2026 23:48:19 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] openarc: media: decode H.264 and AAC only with the platform
 decoders

Open Arc's v1 builds ship without patent-encumbered software decoders
(decision Q6: proprietary_codecs = false). Plan task C18 studies playing
H.264, HEVC and AAC by handing decoding to macOS (VideoToolbox and
AudioToolbox) while bundling no software decoder for them.

Upstream ties the two together: proprietary_codecs (needed for MP4/MSE
demuxing of these formats) requires ffmpeg_branding = "Chrome", whose
FFmpeg carries the H.264 and AAC decoders, and AudioToolboxAudioDecoder
only takes xHE-AAC, so plain AAC-LC and HE-AAC can only be decoded by
FFmpeg. This adds a build argument,
media_proprietary_decoders_platform_only (default false; every change
compiles away without it). With it on, on macOS only:

- GN: no FFmpegVideoDecoder (enable_ffmpeg_video_decoders = false), no
  OpenH264 (media_use_openh264 = false), and ffmpeg_branding must be
  "Chromium" (the upstream assert is inverted for this mode). Exported as
  the MEDIA_PROPRIETARY_DECODERS_PLATFORM_ONLY build flag.
- AudioToolboxAudioDecoder decodes every AAC profile: MPEG-4 AAC with the
  esds cookie (macOS works out LC / HE-AAC / HE-AAC v2), USAC for xHE-AAC.
  ADTS headers that frame an access unit (the MSE MP4 parser prepends
  them; the ADTS and MPEG-2 TS parsers pass them through) are stripped.
  Loudness and DRC settings stay xHE-AAC only.
- GpuMojoMediaClientMac reports {AAC, kUnknown} as supported.
- supported_types.cc answers H.264 and AAC from what the GPU process
  reported instead of "always", so canPlayType / isTypeSupported say no
  when there is no platform decoder (sites then pick VP9 / AV1).
- FFmpeg glue for src= playback: FFmpeg only demuxes AAC and H.264 here,
  so an unset AAC sample format becomes planar float (and skips the
  bytes-per-sample DCHECK) and an unset H.264 pixel format becomes I420,
  as upstream already does for HEVC; "aac" leaves the FFmpeg decoder
  allowlist.

Verified on Apple silicon with out/Release_codecs (proprietary_codecs =
true, ffmpeg_branding = "Chromium", the new argument on): no
ff_h264/hevc/aac decoders or parsers, no OpenH264 and no
FFmpegVideoDecoder in OpenArcCore; H.264/AAC and HEVC/AAC MP4 (src=)
and fMP4 (MSE) all play. Notes: chromium-bridge/CODECS.md in the Open
Arc repository. Patent licensing questions are left to counsel.
